{"ts": 0.22932, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;97mWhere this lives for real\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nThe prompt went back because each screen starts a fresh shell. A real\r\n", "len": 111}
{"ts": 0.229334, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "terminal reads one file when it starts, and settings there last:\r\n\r\n  ~/.bashrc     if your login shell is bash\r\n  ~/.zshrc      if it is zsh\r\n  ~/.bash_profile   on macOS with bash\r\n\r\nA line like  \u001b[92mPS1='me> '\u001b[0m  in that file gives you your own prompt every\r\ntime. Edit it in a normal terminal, not here; the tutor never touches it.\r\n\r\n\u001b[93m> Type \u001b[92mnext\u001b[93m for the task.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n", "len": 390}
{"ts": 0.233086, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;90mnext\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(go on)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mshow\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(this screen again)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mprev\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(back)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mquit\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(save and leave)\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 159}
